+### Packages inside an image (SBOM)
+
+Every scan also keeps the image's packages: Trivy lists each package it
+finds (`--list-all-pkgs`) - system packages and language libraries -
+with its version, type (`debian`, `alpine`, `python-pkg`, `gobinary`,
+`node-pkg`, ...) and package URL, at most 10,000 per image
+([`app/services/docker_sbom.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/services/docker_sbom.py)).
+They are replaced with each scan Trivy answered; images scanned before
+0.133.0 get theirs with their next scan.
+
+- **An image's page** shows how many packages of which type, and
+  **Download CycloneDX** (`machine.view`) gives them as a CycloneDX 1.6
+  JSON file for tools that take an SBOM.
+- **Security → Package search** (`/security/packages`) also lists the
+  packages inside the machines' scanned images (*In Docker images*:
+  machine, image, package, version, type; the source filter *Docker
+  images* shows only those) - which images carry `openssl 3.0.x`, also
+  for a vulnerability without a CVE yet. Images are matched by the
+  **start** of the package name (at least 2 characters, case-insensitive,
+  up to 500 rows), through an index, so the search stays fast with
+  millions of rows; scoped to the machines the account can see.
+
